  "dct_title_s": "Scotia regnum / Amstelodami, Apud Ioannem Ianssonium.",
  "dct_description_sm": [
    "Relief shown pictorially.; Inset map of Orcades Insvlae in upper right corner, 11 x 7 cm.; Title cartouche is topped with the Scottish coat of arms (a lion), flanked by two unicorns. There are two flags and a lion wearing a helmet with a cross on it and holding a sword and a scepter. Beneath the title are two sheep with fish tails.; There are ships in the ocean, and another coat of arms above the title cartouche.; This state was published in atlases by Jan Jansson and Henricus Hondius in 1636, 1637, and 1680.; From the Appendix Atlas of the British Isles and Northern Europe, title created to represent a unique collection within the Clark Library, University of Michigan.",
